@startuml sd-aircraft-grounding
skinparam style strictuml
autonumber
title SD - Aircraft grounding by event (work queue fo.grounding)

actor "ATCC / Maintenance" as User
participant "Aircraft Service" as AC
box "RabbitMQ cluster" #FFF8E8
participant "aircraft.events" as EX
queue "fo.grounding\n(shared, quorum)" as QG
queue "fo.aircraft.fo-1 /\nfo.aircraft.fo-2" as QA
end box
box "ONE FO replica (competing consumers)" #F4F7FF
participant "GroundingHandler" as GH
participant "FlightCommandService" as Svc
database "Replica DB" as DB
end box
participant "flights.events" as FEX

User -> AC : PATCH /api/aircraft-models/instances/{reg}/status\n(UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
AC -> EX : AircraftStatusChanged(reg, ACTIVE -> UNDER_MAINTENANCE)\n(via the Aircraft outbox)
EX -> QA : aircraft.# (every FO replica updates AircraftRef)
EX -> QG : aircraft.status-changed (ONE copy for the whole FO service)
QG -> GH : deliver (only one of FO-1 / FO-2 gets it)
activate GH
alt new status is ACTIVE
  GH -> QG : basicAck (nothing to do)
else not ACTIVE
  GH -> DB : BEGIN; processed_event(consumer = "fo.grounding", eventId)\n(key per consumer: the same event is also projected by fo.aircraft.*)
  GH -> DB : UPDATE aircraft_ref SET status (from the event payload)
  GH -> DB : future flights of reg with status SCHEDULED / DELAYED
  loop each affected flight (ordered by scheduled date)
    GH -> DB : candidates = aircraft_ref WHERE status = ACTIVE\nAND seats >= route.minimumCapacity AND range >= route.distance\nORDER BY registration_number
    GH -> GH : first candidate without a 2 h conflict
    alt free candidate found
      GH -> Svc : reassignAircraft(flight, candidate)
      Svc -> DB : revision + 1; INSERT outbox FlightReassigned
    else no candidate
      GH -> Svc : changeStatus(flight, DELAYED, reason = NO_REPLACEMENT_AIRCRAFT)
      Svc -> DB : revision + 1; INSERT outbox FlightStatusChanged
    end
  end
  GH -> DB : COMMIT
  GH -> QG : basicAck
end
deactivate GH
DB -> FEX : OutboxRelay publishes FlightReassigned / FlightStatusChanged
FEX -> QA : (fo.flights.*) every replica updates replicas, views and moods

== Late flight: scheduled on a replica that had not yet seen the grounding ==
note over GH, DB
  FO-2 accepts a flight for reg just before consuming AircraftStatusChanged.
  When any replica applies that FlightScheduled and its local AircraftRef says reg is not ACTIVE,
  it writes a GroundingRequested(reg) command to its outbox\n(flights.events, routing key fo.grounding.requested) -> routed to fo.grounding.
  The handler is idempotent: flights already moved are skipped, so repeated requests are harmless.
end note

== Failures ==
note over QG, GH
  Replica crashes mid-way: transaction rolled back, no ack -> the message is redelivered to the other replica.
  Both FO replicas down: the message waits in fo.grounding (quorum, durable) until one comes back.
  Aircraft Service down after publishing: irrelevant, the event is already in the broker.
end note
@enduml
